id: frighten
name: Frighten
prerequisite: 2+ Skill Ranks in Intimidation
requiresSkill: intimidation
requiresRanks: 2
# "Session Limit: Infinite."
sessionLimit: infinite
timeCost: Instant
# "Target a Character you can see or speak to. Make a Clash (Intimidation vs Intuition/Intimidation)."
clashSkill: intimidation
clashDefenderSkills: intuition, intimidation
# "You cannot target the same Character twice with the Frighten Maneuver in an Adventuring Session (or
# while they are still influenced by its effects)."
oncePerTarget: true
# "If you win, increase your Alarm Rating for that Character by 1 for 1 Day." Alarm Ratings are not in
# this system: said on the card, {challenger} and {defender} named.
clashWinNote: {challenger}'s Alarm Rating for {defender} is 1 higher for 1 Day
source: Core Rule
description: >
  An Intimidation Clash against someone's Intuition or Intimidation: win, and your Alarm Rating for them
  is 1 higher for a day. Once for each Character in an Adventuring Session.
text: >
  Frighten: You scare someone into believing you’re a threat to them.
  –Prerequisite: 2+ Skill Ranks in Intimidation
  –Session Limit: Infinite
  –Time Cost: Instant
  –Effect: Target a Character you can see or speak to. Make a Clash (Intimidation vs
  Intuition/Intimidation) against them. If you win, increase your Alarm Rating for that Character by 1
  for 1 Day. You cannot target the same Character twice with the Frighten Maneuver in an Adventuring
  Session (or while they are still influenced by its effects).

---

# Offered on the Adventure tab to whoever has 2+ Ranks in Intimidation, with no Session Limit. Used at
# the one token targeted - refused if they were already Frightened this Adventuring Session - and the
# Clash card opens at once. Won, the card says the Alarm Rating: those are not built, so keeping it, the
# day it lasts, and a Character still influenced into the next Session are the table's.
